{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>You shall not make.</b> The sense: behold, I sit in heaven, and I spoke with you not through an intermediary. And thus it is written, Face to face YHWH spoke with you (Deuteronomy 5:4). Do not wonder that it is written לא תעשו twice, for such is the way of the eloquence of the Holy Language, like לא תחמוד (you shall not covet), for the meaning is one. And so לא תעשון לכם אתי אלהי כסף ואלהי זהב (you shall not make for yourselves with Me gods of silver and gods of gold) is like 'you shall not make for yourself a carved image or any likeness' (Exodus 20:4). The meaning of תעשו is that you would make forms to receive supernal powers, and you would think that you are doing it for My honor, as if there were intermediaries between Me and you, like the calf that Israel made, for Aaron made it for the honor of HaShem, as I will explain in its place. And because HaShem knew that Israel would make them, He warned them first not to make gods of gold:" "Now the meaning of אתי (with Me) is: I have no need for intermediaries with Me. Therefore, after it, אבוא אליך וברכתיך (I will come to you and bless you). And the sense is: I, in My glory, will come to you:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The parenthetical verse citation (פ' ד) refers to parashah 4 of Exodus, i.e., Exodus 20:4."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:29.912160684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}